eXA1r2VunLQYMgoHBB"}]},{"role":"tool","sequence":16,"content":[{"type":"toolResult","text":"{\"approval_id\":\"appr_5\",\"total_cost_usd_micros\":1760000,\"max_cost_usd_micros\":1760000,\"next\":\"Present this plan to the user and wait for their reply. Do not execute until they approve.\"}","toolCallId":"toolu_015qvEeXA1r2VunLQYMgoHBB","toolName":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_prepare_route","isError":false}]},{"role":"assistant","sequence":17,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"The route is priced and ready, but nothing has run yet. I need your approval to start.\n\n**Route (approval `appr_5`):**\n\n| # | Leg | In | Out (quoted) | Cost |\n|---|-----|----|--------------|------|\n| 1 | Bridge ETH from Ethereum (eth1) to Base (base1), takes about 60s | 0.1 ETH | 0.099833 ETH | $1.40 |\n| 2 | Swap ETH to USDC on Base (base1) | 0.099793 ETH | ≈299.08 USDC | $0.36 |\n\n- **Total cost:** $1.76, under your $8.00 limit.\n- **Why this route:** Swapping on Ethereum first and then bridging the USDC costs more. The Ethereum swap alone costs $3.90, before the bridge fee.\n- **ETH kept for fees:** About 0.00004 ETH of the bridged ETH isn't swapped. Half pays the fee for the Base swap, and the other 0.00002 ETH stays in base1 so that wallet can still make a transaction. Otherwise base1 would hold USDC with no ETH to move it.\n- **After the route:** eth1 keeps 0.05 ETH, minus fees. base1 ends with about 299.08 USDC and 0.00002 ETH.\n\nReply **approve** to run it, **reject** to cancel, or give me a cost cap. The quotes expire after 300s, so I may need to re-quote."}]},{"role":"user","sequence":18,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, go ahead with that plan."}]},{"role":"assistant","sequence":19,"content":[{"type":"toolCall","name":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_execute_leg","arguments":{"quote_id":"q_1","approval_id":"appr_5"},"id":"toolu_01Mp9WokNiaz3W3LwYUGmXn9"}]},{"role":"tool","sequence":20,"content":[{"type":"toolResult","text":"{\"tx_id\":\"tx_6\"}","toolCallId":"toolu_01Mp9WokNiaz3W